<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	The app's entitlements for the custom firmware wrappers (the deb and the .tipa).
	The ordinary sideload .ipa gets a separate file carrying only the App Group
	(if any): verify-ipa.sh checks these entitlements for *absence* there
	and for presence here, because the two archives fail in opposite directions.

	`wiki.qaq.xrash.client` is the private key the daemon's authenticator
	looks for on a peer. Name it after the app, never reuse another app's, and
	never grant it to anything you would not hand a root descriptor to.

	Mach-lookup of `wiki.qaq.xrash.service` is not optional: without it the app
	cannot find the daemon.

	There is no App Group: Xrash embeds no extension that shares a container.

	`platform-application` is the default. It attests "signed as platform",
	not "this client". If it is unused on the app, drop it from the app *and*
	from the authenticator together.

	Add `com.apple.security.iokit-user-client-class` only if the app draws with
	Metal itself (a terminal, an emulator, a renderer). A bootstrap withholds
	the GPU from an ad-hoc signed binary until this entitlement names the
	classes, and the failure is silent: the surface never reports a viewport and
	the view is a blank rectangle while everything behind it works. Classes
	that have been required on device: AGXCommandQueue, AGXDevice,
	AGXDeviceUserClient, AGXSharedUserClient, AGXGLContext,
	AppleParavirtDeviceUserClient (VM GPU), IOAccelContext, IOAccelContext2,
	IOAccelDevice, IOAccelDevice2, IOAccelSharedUserClient,
	IOAccelSharedUserClient2, IOAccelSubmitter2, IOSurfaceRootUserClient,
	IOSurfaceAcceleratorClient, IOMobileFramebufferUserClient,
	AppleJPEGDriverUserClient, IOHIDLibUserClient,
	IOHIDEventServiceFastPathUserClient. Core Image / Vision may also need
	`exception.iokit-user-client-class`.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>application-identifier</key>
	<string>wiki.qaq.xrash</string>
	<key>wiki.qaq.xrash.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.exception.mach-lookup.global-name</key>
	<array>
		<string>wiki.qaq.xrash.service</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.private.security.no-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>platform-application</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
